/*  dirHeadT -- insertAt with where=before on the FIRST LINE of a buffer.

    ⚠ THIS FIXTURE IS RED ON PURPOSE AND IS PINNED TO THE RIGHT ANSWER (H7).
    It is F-67's RESIDUE, and it only became visible on 2026-09-16: until the
    `*where` star landed in incant/directives, where=before never fired at all,
    so the first-line case could not be reached to be wrong.

    THE DEFECT: the payload lands ONE CHARACTER INTO the first line, so the
    buffer reads `hPAYLOAD` / `eadLine alpha` instead of the payload ahead of
    an intact line.

    THE CAUSE IS NAMED AND GRADED, NOT GUESSED -- getMarkLineAt (Instruct.rtn)
    ends its walk with `if lineStart >= start lineStart++;`, and lineStart can
    never be BELOW start, so the ++ always fires. For a line reached by walking
    back to a \n that step is right, because it steps over the newline. For the
    first line the walk stops at start and the step goes into the text.

    PINNED RIGHT RATHER THAN PINNED WRONG, deliberately: the day the repair
    lands this row GRADUATES on its own instead of waiting to be noticed.

    ⚠ IT HAS ITS OWN SAMPLE AND ITS OWN RUN because getFile is once per FIELD
    and the buffer mark only ever ADVANCES -- a head case cannot share a buffer
    with anything, since everything else is forward of it.

    Sentinel at the foot, single stop.  */
Start();
include(directives);

register(Directives);
define
    source="incant/dirHeadSample";
    dHead source fromThis="headLine" toThis='HEAD-PAYLOAD\n' where=before;
    ;

getFile(source);
insertAt(dHead);
print ``"=== head, where=before ===":source:;
print "DIRHEADT SENTINEL":;
stop();
